      "culture": "Bargaining is common in Yemeni markets and souks, especially in Sana'a, for clothing, household goods, and handicrafts. The back-and-forth haggling is expected and friendly. Greet the seller with \"السلام عليكم\" first, then ask the price. A seller who says \"آخر سعر\" is making a final offer, which is usually worth accepting.",
